{"name":"Silestone","hex":"#b29e81","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Countertop","blocks":[{"text":"A countertop, also counter top, counter, benchtop, worktop or kitchen bench, bunker is a raised, firm, flat, and horizontal surface. They are built for work in kitchens or other food preparation areas, bathrooms or lavatories, and workrooms in general. The surface is frequently installed upon and supported by cabinets, positioned at an ergonomic height for the user and the particular task for which it is designed. A countertop may be constructed of various materials with different attributes of functionality, durability and aesthetics, and may have built-in appliances, or accessory items relative to the intended application."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Kitchen_050918_154652.jpg/330px-Kitchen_050918_154652.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Countertop"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Lab_desk.jpg/500px-Lab_desk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Lab_desk.jpg/1280px-Lab_desk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Lab_desk.jpg/500px-Lab_desk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A lab countertop with drawers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALab_desk.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Kitchen_stone_countertops.jpg/500px-Kitchen_stone_countertops.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Kitchen_stone_countertops.jpg/1280px-Kitchen_stone_countertops.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa